course: dictionary
lesson: 10772
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word vacancy is a good example. Read the words around it first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: A job vacancy is a job that is free and waiting for someone to fill it. A hotel vacancy is an empty room. A sign that says «vacancies» means rooms are free, and «no vacancies» means every room is taken.
explain: «Wild hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells one after another; scientists call this a vacancy chain.» The clues are queue, swap and shells. Each crab moves into the shell left empty by the next biggest crab, so a vacancy here is an empty shell waiting to be taken.
explain: Vacancy can also mean emptiness or a lack of thought. This meaning is formal, so you will meet it more in grown-up writing. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A vacancy is a job, place or room that is free and waiting to be filled.
fact: «Vacancies» on a hotel sign means there are empty rooms to book.
fact: «No vacancies» means every room or job is already taken.
fact: Job vacancies are often advertised so that people can apply for them.
fact: A vacancy chain is when each hermit crab moves into the empty shell left by the next biggest crab.
exercise: A hotel sign says «Vacancies». What does it mean? | *There are free rooms to book | The roof needs mending | The hotel is closed for the winter | Every room is full
exercise: «She applied for the vacancy at the library.» What does vacancy mean here? | *A job that is free to be filled | A very long wait | An empty room in the library | A kind of library book
exercise: «Her eyes had a blank vacancy, as if no thought was behind them.» What does vacancy mean here? | A hot summer day | A free room in a hotel | A free job | *Emptiness, with no thought behind it
test: A school advert says «Teacher vacancy». What is it telling you? | *A teaching job is free to apply for | The school has too many teachers | A teacher is missing from class | A new school building is opening
test: «The hotel had no vacancies, so we went to the next town.» What does no vacancies mean? | The hotel is being painted | *Every room is already taken | There are lots of empty rooms | The manager is on holiday
exam: «The vacancy in the team was filled by Maya.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | A large hole in the ground | An empty room | A lack of thought | *A free job or place to fill
